IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tla-dates`
IMPORT `tla-rules`

-- Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) -- the questions of the CLAIMANT.
--
-- SEAT: the individual to whom a right of action accrues and who brings, or proposes to bring, the action -- the injured
-- person, the family member suing under the Fatal Accidents Act 1934 for a death, the personal representative suing for
-- the estate, the survivor of child abuse, a party to a contract or deed, a creditor, a beneficiary of a trust or an
-- estate, a person who paid a tax that was not owed: "By when must I start my action?", "Can I still start it on this
-- day?", "Can I sue at any time for abuse I suffered as a child?", "Can I reopen my old settlement?", "Did their
-- acknowledgement or payment give me more time?", "Can a judge give me more time?". One question (s 35) is asked by the
-- same individual when answering a claim with a counterclaim. The court, the person sued, an institution, an insurer and
-- The Public Trustee get no seat: the court's judgments and orders are asked as facts.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, dates, numbers, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of tla-rules.l4.
-- The time bar is a DEONTIC rule run inside the two "Can I still commence ... on this day" questions; no question takes a
-- DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of Tasmania, CC BY
-- 4.0; not the authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Limitation Act 1974 (Tas): the claimant's questions`

§§ `Where I stand`

@export Am I "under disability" under the Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) s 2(2), (3)? You are while you are under 18, or while you are incapable, because of mental disorder, of managing your property or affairs -- which you are taken to be while you are subject to an assessment or treatment order under the Mental Health Act 2013, or a guardianship or administration order is in force for you. For claims other than personal injury, being under disability when the claim arose gives you 6 years from when it ends (s 26).
GIVEN `am I under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are under 18 years of age
      `am I unable to manage my affairs because of mental disorder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are incapable, because of mental disorder, of managing your property or affairs
      `am I under a mental health order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are subject to an assessment order or a treatment order under the Mental Health Act 2013
      `is a guardianship or administration order in force for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a guardianship order, or an administration order for your estate, is in force under the Guardianship and Administration Act 1995
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I under disability` MEANS
    `s 2(2) -- I am under a disability` `am I under 18` `am I unable to manage my affairs because of mental disorder` `am I under a mental health order` `is a guardianship or administration order in force for me`

@export Am I a "relevant person", so that the time limit for my personal injury claim stops running for now (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) s 26A)? You are while you are under 18 and not in the custody of a "capable parent" (a parent who is not under disability, is not the person you would sue, and cannot be influenced by them not to sue), or while you have been unable to manage your affairs because of mental disorder for 28 days or more in a row and have no one with legal authority to sue for you who is independent of the person you would sue.
GIVEN `am I under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are under 18 years of age
      `am I in a parent's custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in the custody of a parent (including a guardian appointed by deed, will or court order)
      `is that parent under disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that parent is under 18, or unable to manage their own property or affairs because of mental disorder
      `is that parent the person I would sue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that parent is the person you would sue
      `could a parent be influenced not to sue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that parent, or another parent, may be directly or indirectly influenced by the person you would sue not to bring an action for you
      `incapable for 28 days or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been incapable, because of mental disorder, of managing your property or affairs for a continuous period of 28 days or more
      `have I an independent representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone has legal authority to start and run legal actions for you (for example a guardian or administrator) and is not the person you would sue
      `could my representative be influenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that representative may be directly or indirectly influenced by the person you would sue not to bring an action for you
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I a relevant person whose time is suspended` MEANS
    `s 26A(4) -- I am a relevant person` `am I under 18` `am I in a parent's custody` `is that parent under disability` `is that parent the person I would sue` `could a parent be influenced not to sue` `incapable for 28 days or more` `have I an independent representative` `could my representative be influenced`

§§ `Personal injury and death claims`

@export As the personal representative of someone who has died, what is my "date of discoverability" for the estate's personal injury claim (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) s 5A(6))? It is the earliest of: the day the deceased knew the injury had occurred, was caused by the person to be sued and was serious enough to sue for; and the later of the day you were appointed and the day you first knew or ought to have known of it. The 3-year time limit counts from that day.
GIVEN `did the deceased know` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the deceased person, before dying, knew that the personal injury had occurred, was attributable to the conduct of the person to be sued, and was sufficiently significant to warrant bringing proceedings
      `day the deceased knew` IS A DATE @desc The day the deceased person first knew all three of those things (any date if they did not)
      `day I was appointed` IS A DATE @desc The day you were appointed personal representative (executor or administrator)
      `day I knew or ought to have known` IS A DATE @desc The day you first knew, or ought to have known, that the injury had occurred, was attributable to the person to be sued and was serious enough to warrant proceedings
GIVETH A DATE
`What is my date of discoverability as personal representative` MEANS
    `s 5A(6) -- the date of discoverability for a personal representative` `did the deceased know` `day the deceased knew` `day I was appointed` `day I knew or ought to have known`

@export Can a judge extend the time for my personal injury or death claim to 6 years from my date of discoverability (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) s 5A(5), s 38A(3))? A judge may, if he or she considers it just and reasonable -- except where your claim arose before 1 July 2018 and your date of discoverability was more than 3 years before that day (before 1 July 2015).
GIVEN `did my claim arise before 1 July 2018` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your cause of action accrued (usually: you were injured, or the death occurred) before 1 July 2018
      `my date of discoverability` IS A DATE @desc The day you knew or ought to have known that the injury or death had occurred, was attributable to the conduct of the person you would sue and (for an injury) was serious enough to warrant proceedings
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can a judge extend my time to 6 years` MEANS
    `s 5A(5) -- a judge may extend my period to 6 years` `did my claim arise before 1 July 2018` `my date of discoverability`

@export By when must I start my court action for personal injury, or for a death under the Fatal Accidents Act 1934 (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) ss 5A, 5B, 26A, 32, 38, 38A)? Within 3 years beginning on your date of discoverability (6 years if a judge has extended it), with the clock stopped while you are a minor without a capable parent, or unable to manage your affairs for 28 days or more without an independent representative; never if the claim arises from sexual or serious physical abuse of you as a minor; and not before you discover any fraud or mistake. A time limit in another Act (for example workers compensation or motor accident schemes) applies instead (s 38).
GIVEN `does another Act set the time limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another Act sets the time limit for this action (if so, this Act does not apply: s 38)
      `is it a child abuse claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim arises from or relates to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse (or psychological abuse from either) of the injured or deceased person as a minor (s 5B; see the child abuse question)
      `my date of discoverability` IS A DATE @desc The day you knew or ought to have known that the injury or death had occurred, was attributable to the conduct of the person you would sue and (for an injury) was serious enough to warrant proceedings; for an estate, use the personal representative question
      `has a judge extended it to 6 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a judge has extended the period to 6 years under s 5A(5) as just and reasonable
      `did my claim arise before 1 July 2018` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cause of action accrued before 1 July 2018
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The injured person's date of birth
      `was I a minor without a capable parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after your date of discoverability, there was a time when you were under 18 and not in the custody of a capable parent (see the relevant person question)
      `day that began` IS A DATE @desc The first day of that time (any date if none)
      `has that ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that time has ended before your 18th birthday (if not, it ends when you turn 18)
      `last day of that` IS A DATE @desc The last day of that time (any date if it has not ended)
      `was I incapable without an independent representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after your date of discoverability, there was a time when you were incapable, because of mental disorder, of managing your affairs, with no independent legal representative (see the relevant person question)
      `day incapacity began` IS A DATE @desc The first day of that time (any date if none)
      `has incapacity ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that time has ended
      `last day of incapacity` IS A DATE @desc The last day of that time (any date if it has not ended)
      `fraud or mistake` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action is based on the fraud of the person you would sue (or their agent), the claim was concealed by that fraud, or the action is for relief from the consequences of a mistake
      `has it been discovered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you have discovered the fraud or mistake, or could have with reasonable diligence
      `day it was discovered` IS A DATE @desc The day you discovered it, or could with reasonable diligence have discovered it (any date if not)
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`By when must I commence my injury or death action` MEANS
    `the time limit for the injury claim` (`The injury claim` WITH
        `injury: another Act sets the period`   IS `does another Act set the time limit`
        `injury: child abuse action under s 5B` IS `is it a child abuse claim`
        `injury: discoverability day`           IS `my date of discoverability`
        `injury: extension granted`             IS `has a judge extended it to 6 years`
        `injury: accrued before 1 July 2018`    IS `did my claim arise before 1 July 2018`
        `injury: birth day`                     IS `my date of birth`
        `injury: minor spell`                   IS `was I a minor without a capable parent`
        `injury: minor spell first day`         IS `day that began`
        `injury: minor spell has ended`         IS `has that ended`
        `injury: minor spell last day`          IS `last day of that`
        `injury: incapacity spell`              IS `was I incapable without an independent representative`
        `injury: incapacity spell first day`    IS `day incapacity began`
        `injury: incapacity spell has ended`    IS `has incapacity ended`
        `injury: incapacity spell last day`     IS `last day of incapacity`
        `injury: fraud or mistake`              IS `fraud or mistake`
        `injury: fraud discovered`              IS `has it been discovered`
        `injury: fraud discovery day`           IS `day it was discovered`)

@export If I start my court action for personal injury or a death on a given day, is it in time (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) ss 5A, 5B, 26A, 32, 38)? Yes on or before the last day, or at any time where no limit applies or the clock has not started or is stopped; no after the last day, unless a judge extends it (s 5A(5)).
GIVEN `does another Act set the time limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another Act sets the time limit for this action (if so, this Act does not apply: s 38)
      `is it a child abuse claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim arises from or relates to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse (or psychological abuse from either) of the injured or deceased person as a minor (s 5B)
      `my date of discoverability` IS A DATE @desc The day you knew or ought to have known that the injury or death had occurred, was attributable to the conduct of the person you would sue and (for an injury) was serious enough to warrant proceedings
      `has a judge extended it to 6 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a judge has extended the period to 6 years under s 5A(5) as just and reasonable
      `did my claim arise before 1 July 2018` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cause of action accrued before 1 July 2018
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The injured person's date of birth
      `was I a minor without a capable parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after your date of discoverability, there was a time when you were under 18 and not in the custody of a capable parent
      `day that began` IS A DATE @desc The first day of that time (any date if none)
      `has that ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that time has ended before your 18th birthday (if not, it ends when you turn 18)
      `last day of that` IS A DATE @desc The last day of that time (any date if it has not ended)
      `was I incapable without an independent representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after your date of discoverability, there was a time when you were incapable, because of mental disorder, of managing your affairs, with no independent legal representative
      `day incapacity began` IS A DATE @desc The first day of that time (any date if none)
      `has incapacity ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that time has ended
      `last day of incapacity` IS A DATE @desc The last day of that time (any date if it has not ended)
      `fraud or mistake` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action is based on the fraud of the person you would sue (or their agent), the claim was concealed by that fraud, or the action is for relief from the consequences of a mistake
      `has it been discovered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you have discovered the fraud or mistake, or could have with reasonable diligence
      `day it was discovered` IS A DATE @desc The day you discovered it, or could with reasonable diligence have discovered it (any date if not)
      `day I commence` IS A DATE @desc The day you file (or would file) the writ or other originating process starting the action
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I still commence my injury or death action on this day` MEANS
    `an action commenced on` `day I commence` `is in time under` (`By when must I commence my injury or death action` `does another Act set the time limit` `is it a child abuse claim` `my date of discoverability` `has a judge extended it to 6 years` `did my claim arise before 1 July 2018` `my date of birth` `was I a minor without a capable parent` `day that began` `has that ended` `last day of that` `was I incapable without an independent representative` `day incapacity began` `has incapacity ended` `last day of incapacity` `fraud or mistake` `has it been discovered` `day it was discovered`)

§§ `Child abuse claims`
-- Arises only for a person abused as a minor ("Has this happened to you?").

@export Can I bring my claim for injury from abuse I suffered as a child at any time, however long ago (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) s 5B)? Yes for damages for personal injury, or a Fatal Accidents Act 1934 claim for a death, arising from or related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse of the person as a minor, including psychological abuse arising from it. Otherwise the ordinary time limit applies (s 5A). A court keeps its powers, for example to stop a case that cannot be tried fairly (s 5B(3)).
GIVEN `is it a damages claim for injury or death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for damages for personal injury to you, or a Fatal Accidents Act 1934 claim for a death
      `what was the abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc What the abuse was: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; psychological abuse arising from sexual or serious physical abuse; or other abuse or harm
      `was I a minor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or the person who died) were under 18 when the abuse happened
      `did the injury arise from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury (or death) arose from or was related to that abuse
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I bring my child abuse action at any time` MEANS
    `s 5B -- my action may be brought at any time` `is it a damages claim for injury or death` `what was the abuse` `was I a minor` `did the injury arise from it`

@export I settled a claim for abuse I suffered as a child: can I now ask a court to set the settlement aside and sue (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) s 5C)? You can if you settled before 1 July 2018 after a time limit had already expired on your claim, and the abuse was sexual or serious physical abuse (or psychological abuse from it) that was unlawful when it happened. The court sets it aside if it is in the interests of justice. Not for an offer of redress accepted under the National Redress Scheme.
GIVEN `what was the abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc What the abuse was: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; psychological abuse arising from sexual or serious physical abuse; or other abuse or harm
      `was I a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were under 18 when the abuse happened
      `was it lawful at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act was lawful at the time it occurred
      `day I settled` IS A DATE @desc The day the settlement agreement was made
      `had a time limit expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when you settled, a limitation period that applied to your claim had already expired
      `was it a National Redress Scheme offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the settlement was an offer of redress you accepted under section 42 of the National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth)
      `has the court set it aside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has already ordered, on your application, that the settlement be set aside in the interests of justice
GIVETH A `Settlement outcome`
`What can I do about my earlier child abuse settlement` MEANS
    `s 5C -- what I can do about my earlier settlement` `what was the abuse` `was I a child` `was it lawful at the time` `day I settled` `had a time limit expired` `was it a National Redress Scheme offer` `has the court set it aside`

@export If my old child abuse settlement is set aside and I win, how much of what I was paid under it can the court take into account in my damages (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) s 5C(6), (7))? At most the part that relates to the abuse: all of it if the agreement was only about the abuse; the part it expressly says relates to the abuse; or otherwise half of everything paid. The court does so only if it is just and reasonable.
GIVEN `total paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of all amounts paid to you under the settlement agreement, in dollars
      `was it only about the abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement related solely to the child abuse
      `did it say how much was for the abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement expressly indicated the extent to which it and the amounts paid related to the child abuse
      `amount it said was for the abuse` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the agreement indicated related to the child abuse, in dollars (any number if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much of my earlier settlement can the court take into account` MEANS
    `s 5C(6), (7) -- the most of my earlier payment the court may take into account` `total paid` `was it only about the abuse` `did it say how much was for the abuse` `amount it said was for the abuse`

@export Once my child abuse settlement is set aside, can the other party get back what it paid me because the agreement is void (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) s 5C(5))? No.
GIVEN `has the court set it aside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has ordered under s 5C that the settlement agreement be set aside
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the other party get back what it paid me` MEANS
    `s 5C(5) -- the other party can recover what it paid me because the agreement is void` `has the court set it aside`

§§ `Other claims: contracts, debts, deeds, judgments, trusts, estates, ships and taxes`

@export By when must I start my court action, or is there no time limit (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) ss 4, 8, 24, 25, 25D, 26, 27, 29-32, 38)? Contract and tort (not personal injury), sums due under an Act, arrears of interest, other breach of trust: 6 years; a deed, a judgment, a share of a deceased estate: 12 years; a ship collision claim: 2 years; tax paid that was not owed: 12 months from payment. No limit for a trustee's fraud or trust property the trustee keeps. If you were under 18 or unable to manage your affairs when the claim arose, you have 6 years from when that ends (or your death); a signed acknowledgement or a payment of a debt restarts the time; fraud or mistake delays the start. A time limit in another Act applies instead (s 38).
GIVEN `what kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc What the claim is: contract or tort other than personal injury; a sum recoverable under an Act (not a penalty); a deed; a judgment; arrears of interest; a share in a deceased estate; arrears of interest on a legacy; a beneficiary's claim for the trustee's fraud or for trust property the trustee holds or converted; another breach of trust; against a ship or its owners for another ship's fault; money paid as a tax or under a mistake about a tax law, from the Crown or a public authority; or another kind (not answered)
      `does another Act set the time limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another Act sets the time limit for this action (if so, this Act does not apply: s 38)
      `day it accrued` IS A DATE @desc The day the right of action accrued to you: for a judgment, the day it became enforceable; for interest, the day it fell due; for an estate share, the day you became entitled to receive it; for a future trust interest, the day it fell into possession; for a ship claim, the day the damage, loss or injury was caused; for a tax, the day you paid it
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `was I incapable when it accrued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the day it accrued, you were incapable, because of mental disorder, of managing your property or affairs (see the disability question)
      `has that incapacity ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that incapacity has ended
      `day it ended` IS A DATE @desc The day that incapacity ended (any date if it has not)
      `did it first accrue to someone before me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the right first accrued to someone not under disability through whom you claim (for example a person whose rights you inherited)
      `have I died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person to whom it accrued has died (answer for them if you act for their estate)
      `day of death` IS A DATE @desc The day of that death (any date if none)
      `was a notice to proceed served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person you would sue has served a notice to proceed under s 27 (on The Public Trustee, the Crown Solicitor, or your guardian or carer)
      `day of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice to proceed was served (any date if none)
      `fraud or mistake` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action is based on the fraud of the person you would sue (or their agent), the claim was concealed by that fraud, or the action is for relief from the consequences of a mistake
      `has it been discovered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you have discovered the fraud or mistake, or could have with reasonable diligence
      `day it was discovered` IS A DATE @desc The day you discovered it, or could with reasonable diligence have discovered it (any date if not)
      `is it a debt or fixed sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for a debt or other fixed (liquidated) sum of money
      `what did they give` IS A `Kind of acknowledgement` @desc Whether the person liable acknowledged your claim or paid something: a written, signed acknowledgement; a payment in respect of the claim; an acknowledgement not in writing or not signed; or nothing of that kind (if more than one, the latest)
      `day they gave it` IS A DATE @desc The day of that acknowledgement or (latest) payment (any date if none)
      `was it the person I would sue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was made by the person you would sue, or their agent (rather than someone else liable for the same debt)
      `is it recoverable as an overpayment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a tax: whether the amount is recoverable as an overpayment under the taxing law (or would be if the tax were valid or the amount not paid by mistake)
      `has the court extended the ship claim time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a ship claim: whether the court has extended the 2-year period under s 8(4)
      `extended to` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period as the court extended it (any date if not)
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`By when must I commence my action` MEANS
    `the time limit for` (`The claim` WITH
        `claim kind`                              IS `what kind of claim`
        `another Act sets the period`             IS `does another Act set the time limit`
        `accrual day`                             IS `day it accrued`
        `claimant birth day`                      IS `my date of birth`
        `incapable at accrual`                    IS `was I incapable when it accrued`
        `incapacity has ended`                    IS `has that incapacity ended`
        `incapacity end day`                      IS `day it ended`
        `first accrued to a predecessor not under disability` IS `did it first accrue to someone before me`
        `claimant has died`                       IS `have I died`
        `claimant death day`                      IS `day of death`
        `notice to proceed served`                IS `was a notice to proceed served`
        `notice to proceed day`                   IS `day of the notice`
        `fraud or mistake`                        IS `fraud or mistake`
        `fraud discovered`                        IS `has it been discovered`
        `fraud discovery day`                     IS `day it was discovered`
        `claim is for a debt or fixed sum`        IS `is it a debt or fixed sum`
        `acknowledgement given`                   IS `what did they give`
        `acknowledgement day`                     IS `day they gave it`
        `acknowledged by the person I would sue`  IS `was it the person I would sue`
        `recoverable as an overpayment`           IS `is it recoverable as an overpayment`
        `court extended the ship claim period`    IS `has the court extended the ship claim time`
        `ship claim extended to`                  IS `extended to`)

@export If I start my court action (other than for personal injury or a death) on a given day, is it in time (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) ss 4, 8, 24, 25, 25D, Part III)? Yes on or before the last day, or at any time where no limit applies or none has yet been fixed; no after the last day. Before the claim has accrued the Act does not answer.
GIVEN `what kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc What the claim is: contract or tort other than personal injury; a sum recoverable under an Act; a deed; a judgment; arrears of interest; a share in a deceased estate; arrears of interest on a legacy; a beneficiary's claim for the trustee's fraud or trust property; another breach of trust; a ship claim; money paid as a tax; or another kind (not answered)
      `does another Act set the time limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another Act sets the time limit for this action (if so, this Act does not apply: s 38)
      `day it accrued` IS A DATE @desc The day the right of action accrued to you (see the time limit question)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `was I incapable when it accrued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the day it accrued, you were incapable, because of mental disorder, of managing your property or affairs
      `has that incapacity ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that incapacity has ended
      `day it ended` IS A DATE @desc The day that incapacity ended (any date if it has not)
      `did it first accrue to someone before me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the right first accrued to someone not under disability through whom you claim
      `have I died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person to whom it accrued has died
      `day of death` IS A DATE @desc The day of that death (any date if none)
      `was a notice to proceed served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person you would sue has served a notice to proceed under s 27
      `day of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice to proceed was served (any date if none)
      `fraud or mistake` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action is based on fraud, the claim was concealed by fraud, or the action is for relief from a mistake
      `has it been discovered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you have discovered the fraud or mistake, or could have with reasonable diligence
      `day it was discovered` IS A DATE @desc The day you discovered it, or could with reasonable diligence have discovered it (any date if not)
      `is it a debt or fixed sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for a debt or other fixed (liquidated) sum of money
      `what did they give` IS A `Kind of acknowledgement` @desc A written, signed acknowledgement; a payment in respect of the claim; an acknowledgement not in writing or not signed; or nothing of that kind
      `day they gave it` IS A DATE @desc The day of that acknowledgement or (latest) payment (any date if none)
      `was it the person I would sue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was made by the person you would sue, or their agent
      `is it recoverable as an overpayment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a tax: whether the amount is recoverable as an overpayment under the taxing law
      `has the court extended the ship claim time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a ship claim: whether the court has extended the 2-year period under s 8(4)
      `extended to` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period as the court extended it (any date if not)
      `day I commence` IS A DATE @desc The day you file (or would file) the writ or other originating process starting the action
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I still commence my action on this day` MEANS
    IF `day I commence` `is before` `day it accrued`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `an action commenced on` `day I commence` `is in time under` (`By when must I commence my action` `what kind of claim` `does another Act set the time limit` `day it accrued` `my date of birth` `was I incapable when it accrued` `has that incapacity ended` `day it ended` `did it first accrue to someone before me` `have I died` `day of death` `was a notice to proceed served` `day of the notice` `fraud or mistake` `has it been discovered` `day it was discovered` `is it a debt or fixed sum` `what did they give` `day they gave it` `was it the person I would sue` `is it recoverable as an overpayment` `has the court extended the ship claim time` `extended to`)

@export Did the written acknowledgement or payment I received restart the time limit for my claim (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) ss 29-31)? For a debt or other fixed sum, or a claim to a deceased estate, the right is treated as accruing afresh on the day of a signed written acknowledgement by the person liable, or of a payment -- even after the time had run out, against the one who made it. An unsigned or spoken acknowledgement does not count; a payment by someone else liable counts against you only if made before your time ran out.
GIVEN `is it a debt, fixed sum or estate claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is for a debt or other fixed (liquidated) sum of money, or to the personal estate of a deceased person or a share in it
      `what did they give` IS A `Kind of acknowledgement` @desc A written, signed acknowledgement of your claim; a payment in respect of it (principal or interest); an acknowledgement not in writing or not signed; or nothing of that kind
      `day they gave it` IS A DATE @desc The day of that acknowledgement or payment
      `was it the person I would sue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was made by the person you would sue, or their agent (rather than someone else liable for the same debt)
      `had my time already run out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was made after the time limit for your claim had already expired
GIVETH A `Acknowledgement effect`
`Did their acknowledgement or payment restart my time` MEANS
    `ss 29-31 -- the effect of the acknowledgement or payment` `is it a debt, fixed sum or estate claim` `what did they give` `day they gave it` `was it the person I would sue` `had my time already run out`

@export Can I sue the Crown or a public authority to get back money I paid as a tax, or under a mistake about whether a tax law was valid (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) s 25C)? Only if you satisfy the court that you have not passed (and will not pass) any of the cost on to anyone else, or that you have reimbursed, or contracted to reimburse, everyone you passed it on to. The time limit is 12 months from payment and cannot be extended (ss 25D, 25E).
GIVEN `have I passed it on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have charged to or recovered from anyone else, or will, any amount for the whole or part of what you paid
      `have I reimbursed them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you have reimbursed, or contracted to reimburse, each of them for the amount you claim
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I sue to recover the tax I paid` MEANS
    `s 25C -- my action to recover the tax is maintainable` `have I passed it on` `have I reimbursed them`

§§ `When I answer a claim`
-- Arises only when someone has sued you ("Has someone started an action against you?").

@export I have been sued and want to counterclaim or set off a claim of my own: on what day is my claim taken to have been started, for the time limit (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) s 35)? On the day the action against you was started, even if you plead it later.
GIVEN `day the action against me began` IS A DATE @desc The day the action in which you plead your set-off or counterclaim was commenced
GIVETH A DATE
`When is my counterclaim taken to have been commenced` MEANS
    `s 35 -- the day my counterclaim is taken to be commenced` `day the action against me began`
